{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794544202277,"sessionID":"ses_e2cd4f3cfffeelBSvDjDgyOLSn","part":{"partID":"prt_1d32b70310011eBMPw7WPZLZLb","sessionID":"ses_e2cd4f3cfffeelBSvDjDgyOLSn","messageID":"msg_1d32b6027001RO4RFtvrlYW8Wg","type":"tool","id":"call_f0b6af11a5f44d52abca73a3","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/012-plain-offer-reach/tasks.md","limit":120},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/012-plain-offer-reach/tasks.md, lines 1-120\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Tasks: Phase 12: plain-offer-reach\"\n3: description: \"Ordered worker-sized tasks in five waves: name the matched doctor command in the hand-off, add sk-doc paraphrase aliases, label a hub that needs a mode, pair each deep mode with a scorer anchor and a hub alias and, only when the floors stay put, anchor three create rows. Each wave ends with a recapture and a floor check.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"plain offer reach tasks\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Tasks: Phase 12: plain-offer-reach\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n17: ## Task Notation\n18: \n19: | Prefix | Meaning |\n20: |--------|---------|\n21: | `[ ]` | Pending |\n22: | `[x]` | Completed |\n23: | `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n24: | `[B]` | Blocked |\n25: | `[C]` | Coordinator task: a decision, a revert, a live hook run or an operator step. No worker runs it |\n26: \n27: **Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n28: \n29: Every command runs from the repository root unless a task says otherwise.\n30: - `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. `TC` is `npm run typecheck` in `ADV`, which must exit 0. `BLD` is `npm run build` in `ADV`, which must exit 0. `SP` is this phase's `scratch/` folder.\n31: - `DH` is `$ADV/lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.ts` and `DHT` its test `$ADV/tests/doctor-helper-handoff.vitest.ts`. `VDHT` is `npx vitest run tests/doctor-helper-handoff.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n32: - `FU` is `$ADV/lib/scorer/fusion.ts`. `FHT` is `$ADV/tests/scorer/doctor-handoff-command.vitest.ts` (new) and `VFHT` is `npx vitest run tests/scorer/doctor-handoff-command.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n33: - `DP` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/doctor-prompts.jsonl`. `VDS` is `npx vitest run tests/doctor-routing-slice.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n34: - `CA` is `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` and `CAT` its test `$ADV/tests/command-attach.vitest.ts`. `VCA` is `npx vitest run tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` in `ADV`. `DBC` is `node $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs --check | jq -r .status`, which must print `fresh`.\n35: - `SCH` is `$ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` and `VSCH` is `npx vitest run tests/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.vitest.ts` in `ADV`. `SUB` is `$ADV/lib/subprocess.ts`.\n36: - `AR` is `$ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` and `ARC` its test `$ADV/tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts`. `VARC` is `npx vitest run tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n37: - `HFB` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts` and `HFT` its test `$ADV/tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts`. `VHFT` is `npx vitest run tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n38: - `RD` is `$ADV/lib/render.ts` and `GT` is `$ADV/tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts`. `VGT` is `npx vitest run tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts tests/command-head-length.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n39: - `EX` is `$ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/explicit.ts`. `VEX` is `npx vitest run tests/command-bridge-resolution-guard.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n40: - `HRD` is `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/hub-router.json` and `HRL` is `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/hub-router.json`. `CF_DOC` is `.skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/007-sk-doc/fixtures/canary-cases.v1.json` and `CF_LOOP` is `.skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/002-system-deep-loop/fixtures/canary-cases.v1.json`.\n41: - `MS` is `.skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/013-live-activation/activation` (the served manifests) and `MA` is `specs/sk-doc/z_archive/019-skill-routing-refactor/015-router-unification-program/013-live-activation/activation` (their authored twins).\n42: - `REFRESH <hub>` is three commands in order: `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route-manifest.cjs refresh --hub <hub> --skill-root .skilled/skills/<hub>`, then `cp $MS/<hub>/manifest.json $MA/<hub>/manifest.json`, then `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route-guard.cjs --json | jq .failures`, which must print `0`.\n43: - `HUBOK <hub>` is four checks: `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route-manifest.cjs freshness --hub <hub> --skill-root .skilled/skills/<hub> | jq -r .causeCode` prints `fresh`, `cmp $MS/<hub>/manifest.json $MA/<hub>/manifest.json` prints nothing, `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route-sync.cjs --check | tail -1` prints `all 55 served copies match their authored files` and `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/<hub> | tail -1` prints a line that starts with `OK: parent-skill-check`.\n44: - `BINT` is `node --test .skilled/bin/tests/compiled-route-*.test.cjs`, which must print `ℹ fail 0`.\n45: - `CAP` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`. `BASE` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json`. `CORPUS` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl`. `RS` is `npx vitest run tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n46: - `RT` is a shell function that prints the compiled route of every non-holdout corpus row and every canary prompt on one hub, as `<id><TAB>{\"action\":...,\"t\":[...]}`, and never prints a prompt. Define it in the shell first: `RT() { { jq -r 'select(.split!=\"holdout\") | [.id, .prompt] | @tsv' \"$CORPUS\"; jq -r '.cases[] | select(.prompt) | [\"canary:\" + .id, .prompt] | @tsv' \"$2\"; } | while IFS=$'\\t' read -r id p; do printf '%s\\t%s\\n' \"$id\" \"$(printf '%s' \"$p\" | node .skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub \"$1\" --prompt-stdin | jq -c '{action, t: [.targets[]? | .workflowMode]}')\"; done; }`. Call it as `RT sk-doc $CF_DOC` (154 lines) or `RT system-deep-loop $CF_LOOP` (139 lines).\n47: - `FLOOR` is `node $CAP | jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer'`, which must print at least `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` and exactly `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`.\n48: - `TYPED` is `node $CAP | jq -c '.attachedMetrics.false_offer_attached, .attachedMetrics.typed'`, which must print exactly `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}` and the typed line in `$SP/before.txt` (`{\"own\":24,\"attached\":20,\"combined\":44,\"total\":44}` once phase 011 is committed).\n49: - `PLAIN` is `node $CAP | jq -c '.attachedMetrics.plain.tune, .attachedMetrics.plain.holdout'`. It is a measurement, not a gate. The holdout line is a count and never a prompt.\n50: - `EVAL` is `node $ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs | jq -c '[.metrics.full_corpus_top1.correct,.metrics.holdout_top1.correct,.metrics.ambiguity_top1.correct,.metrics.gold_none_false_fire.value]'`, which must print numbers no lower than `[159,50,20]` and no lower than its line in `$SP/before.txt`, with the fourth no higher than 5.\n51: - `PY` is `python3 $ADV/tests/python/test_skill_advisor.py`, which must exit 0. `PAR` is `npx vitest run tests/parity/python-ts-parity.vitest.ts` in `ADV`, which must report 0 failed. `SUITE` is `npx vitest run` in `ADV`, whose `Test Files` and `Tests` summary lines must name no `failed` count.\n52: - `FLOORCHECK <X>` is: run `BLD`, then `FLOOR`, `TYPED`, `PLAIN`, `EVAL`, `TC`, `PY`, `PAR`, `RS`, `VDS`, `BINT`, `GUARD` (`node .skilled/bin/compiled-route-guard.cjs --json | jq .failures`) and `SUITE`, and write into `$SP/after-<X>.txt` one line per output line, each prefixed with the shorthand name and a colon, such as `FLOOR: {\"count\":0,\"total\":35}` or `TC: exit 0`. For the test runners write the summary line. It passes when every gate above prints what it must. `$SP/before.txt` uses the same format.\n53: \n54: Rules for every task:\n55: - Each task is one change to the files it names. A task that names a module and its test adds the behaviour and the cases that pin it.\n56: - No task reads or prints holdout prompt text. A script filters on `split` before it uses a prompt and prints row ids only. Tune and none rows may be read.\n57: - No code comment may name a spec path, a phase number, a task id, an ADR or a REQ id. State the durable reason instead. T032 checks it.\n58: - No task writes to the home folder, installs anything, adds a dependency, edits `AGENTS.md`, edits a file under `.skilled/commands/create/`, edits a `ROUTER.md` or edits a canary fixture.\n59: - A task that edits a hub `hub-router.json` ends with `REFRESH <hub>` and `HUBOK <hub>` in the same task.\n60: - The brief head keeps the phase 005 form. The `(needs a mode)` label is the one addition, and `GT` is re-pinned in the same task as the renderer.\n61: - A `.md` edit routes through `sk-doc` and a code edit through `sk-code` before the first write. Every task re-reads its anchor text first, because phase 011 edited the same files.\n62: \n63: Worker waves. Tasks in one wave touch different files and can run in parallel. Each task owns the files in parentheses. A wave starts only after the previous wave's last task printed its expected output.\n64: - Wave 0: T001 (`$SP/before.txt`), T002 (`$SP/routes-*-before.tsv`), T003 (`$SP/plain-before.json`). Read-only for the repository.\n65: - Gate: no task from wave A1 on starts before the coordinator confirms that phase 011 is committed, because it edits `CA`, `FU`, `AR`, `SCH`, `CAP` and `BASE`.\n66: - Wave A1: T004 (`DH`, `DHT`).\n67: - Wave A2: T005 (`FU`, `FHT`).\n68: - Wave A3: T006 (`DP`), T007 (the doctor feature catalog page).\n69: - Wave A4: T008 (`BASE`). Wave A5: T009 (`$SP/after-A.txt`).\n70: - Wave B1: T010 (`HRD`, both `sk-doc` manifests). Wave B2: T011 (`BASE`). Wave B3: T012 (`$SP/after-B.txt`).\n71: - Wave C1: T013 (`CA`, `CAT`), T014 (`SCH`), T015 (`SUB`).\n72: - Wave C2: T016 (`AR`, `ARC`), T017 (`RD`, `GT`).\n73: - Wave C3: T018 (`HFB`, `HFT`), T019 (the hook guide). Wave C4: T020 (`$SP/after-C.txt`).\n74: - Wave D1: T021 (`EX`), T022 (`HRL`, both deep-loop manifests). Wave D2: T023 (`BASE`). Wave D3: T024 (`$SP/after-D.txt`). Wave D4: T025 [C].\n75: - Wave E1: T026 (`EX`). Wave E2: T027 (`BASE`). Wave E3: T028 (`$SP/after-E.txt`). Wave E4: T029 [C].\n76: - Verification, one at a time: T030, T031, T032, T033 [C], T034.\n77: \n78: Expected plain tune line (`.attachedMetrics.plain.tune`) per wave. Only the floors are a hard gate:\n79: \n80: | After | own | attached | combined |\n81: |-------|-----|----------|----------|\n82: | Wave 0 | 2 | 7 | 9 |\n83: | A | 7 | 7 | 14 |\n84: | B | 7 | 10 | 17 |\n85: | C | 7 | 10 | 17 |\n86: | D | 7 | 13 | 20 |\n87: | E | 8 | 15 | 23 |\n88: <!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n89: \n90: ---\n91: \n92: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n93: ## Phase 1: Setup\n94: \n95: - [x] T001 Record the before numbers (`$SP/before.txt`). Run `BLD` only if `node $CAP` refuses a stale build, then run `FLOOR`, `TYPED`, `PLAIN`, `EVAL`, `TC`, `PY`, `PAR`, `RS`, `VDS`, `VCA`, `VGT`, `VDHT`, `VARC`, `VHFT`, `VSCH`, `VEX`, `DBC`, `BINT`, `SUITE`, `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route-guard.cjs --json | jq .failures`, `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route-sync.cjs --check | tail -1` and `HUBOK sk-doc` and `HUBOK system-deep-loop`, and write them into `before.txt` in the `FLOORCHECK` line format. Verify: `FLOOR` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `TYPED` prints `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}` and a typed line, `PLAIN` prints `{\"own\":2,\"attached\":7,\"combined\":9,\"total\":45}` first, `EVAL` prints numbers no lower than `[159,50,20]` with a fourth no higher than 5, `TC` and `PY` exit 0, the guard prints `0` and `wc -l < $SP/before.txt` prints at least 25. When a gate is red here, stop and mark the phase `[B]` with that line, because a red before number cannot be held. When `SUITE` names failed files, list them in `before.txt`, and from then on the `SUITE` gate is \"no failed file outside that list\".\n96: - [x] T002 Record every compiled route before any hub edit (`$SP/routes-sk-doc-before.tsv`, `$SP/routes-deep-loop-before.tsv`). Define `RT` and run `RT sk-doc $CF_DOC > $SP/routes-sk-doc-before.tsv` and `RT system-deep-loop $CF_LOOP > $SP/routes-deep-loop-before.tsv`. Verify: `wc -l < $SP/routes-sk-doc-before.tsv` prints 154, `wc -l < $SP/routes-deep-loop-before.tsv` prints 139, `rg -c 'holdout' $SP/routes-*-before.tsv` prints nothing or 0 for both and `rg -n '^nm-system-deep-loop-01' $SP/routes-deep-loop-before.tsv` prints `nm-system-deep-loop-01\t{\"action\":\"route\",\"t\":[\"research\"]}`.\n97: - [x] T003 Record each plain tune row's state (`$SP/plain-before.json`): run `node $CAP | jq '.attachedMetrics.attachedRows as $a | [.rows | to_entries[] | select(.key | test(\"plain-tune\")) | {id: .key, expected: .value.expected_command, top: .value.top, top1: .value.top1, top3: .value.top3, attached: ($a[.key] // null)}]' > $SP/plain-before.json`. Verify: `jq 'length' $SP/plain-before.json` prints 45, `jq '[.[] | select(.top1)] | length' $SP/plain-before.json` prints 2 and `jq -r '.[] | select(.id==\"cmd-doctor-ci-plain-tune-01\") | .top' $SP/plain-before.json` prints `command-doctor-helper`.\n98: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n99: \n100: ---\n101: \n102: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n103: ## Phase 2: Implementation\n104: \n105: ### Wave A1: the doctor hand-off module\n106: - [x] T004 Return the ranked runnable, add the gerund cue and add a repair request cue (`DH`, `DHT`). In `DH`: (1) in `interface HelperCandidate` add `readonly runnable?: string;` after `readonly command: string;`. (2) In `interface DoctorProblemMatch` add `readonly runnable: string;` after `readonly command: string;`, with the doc comment `` /** The command with its subcommand, such as `/doctor:agents-md check`. */ ``. (3) In `matchDoctorProblem`, change the returned object to `{ command: first.command, runnable: typeof first.runnable === 'string' && first.runnable !== '' ? first.runnable : first.command, score: first.score }`. (4) In `STRONG_PROBLEM_CUE`, add the line `  '\\\\bstopped converg\\\\w*\\\\b',` right after the line that starts `  '\\\\bnever (?:converg`. (5) After the `WEAK_PROBLEM_CUE` declaration add `const GENERIC_REPAIR_CUE = /\\b(?:repair path|i have a problem)\\b/i;` with the comment: a request for a repair route that names no problem the ranker knows still belongs to /doctor:helper, which lists the routes and their reasons, and the two phrases are exact so ordinary work requests never carry them. (6) After `doctorProblemCue` add `export function genericRepairCue(prompt: string): boolean { return GENERIC_REPAIR_CUE.test(prompt); }` with the doc comment `/** True when the prompt asks for a repair route without naming the problem. */`. (7) In the module header, replace `and if it does the advisor offers` and the line after it, `/doctor:helper, which then names the command.`, with `and if it does the advisor offers the command the ranker named, or` and `/doctor:helper when that command asks before it runs.`. In `DHT` add cases: `doctorProblemCue('my research loop stopped converging and I cannot see why')` is `'strong'`, `matchDoctorProblem('confirm the AGENTS.md sections in this repo have not drifted', WORKSPACE)?.runnable` is `'/doctor:agents-md check'`, `matchDoctorProblem('show me every GitHub Actions workflow and whether each is enabled', WORKSPACE)?.runn... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n107: \n108: ### Wave A2: the hand-off inserts the named command\n109: - [x] T005 Insert the ranked `run` command instead of the helper (`FU`, `FHT`). In `FU`: (1) add `COMMAND_ROWS` to the import from `'../command-attach.js'` and `genericRepairCue` to the import from `'./doctor-helper-handoff.js'`. (2) Right above the comment block that precedes `export function applyDoctorHelperHandoff(`, add `export function runnableDoctorBridgeId(runnable: string, projection: AdvisorProjection): string | undefined` with this body: for each `[id, row]` of `Object.entries(COMMAND_ROWS)`, skip it unless `id.startsWith(DOCTOR_BRIDGE_PREFIX)`, `row.command === runnable` and `row.policy === 'run'`, and return `id` when `projection.skills.some((skill) => skill.id === id)`. After the loop return `undefined`. Its comment says the ranker names a runnable such as `/doctor:agents-md check`, and this returns that bridge when it runs without asking and the projection holds it. (3) Replace the four comment lines above `applyDoctorHelperHandoff` with: `// A doctor problem described in other words than a bridge's own phrases reaches`, `// no doctor bridge. When none passes and none was typed, /doctor:helper's ranker`, `// decides whether the prompt is a doctor problem. If it is, the command it ranks`, `// first passes when that command runs without asking, and the helper passes`, `// otherwise. A plain request for a repair route with no ranked command and no`, `// passing skill also gets the helper.`. (4) In the function, replace `if (!match) return [...ranked];` with `if (!match && (skillPasses || !genericRepairCue(context.prompt))) return [...ranked];`, and prefix the next condition with `match && ` so it reads `if (match && cue === null && match.score < DOCTOR_HELPER_UNCUED_MIN_SCORE) return [...ranked];`. (5) Before `const existing =` add `const handoffId = (match ? runnableDoctorBridgeId(match.runnable, context.projection) : undefined) ?? DOCTOR_HELPER_BRIDGE_ID;` and `const handoffSkill = context.projection.skills.find((skill) => skill.id === handoffId) ?? he... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n110: \n111: ### Wave A3\n112: - [x] T006 [P] Relabel the three hand-off rows that now get a named command (`DP`). Change exactly three lines and nothing else. In the line with `\"id\":\"doctor-b-helper-handoff-01\"`, replace `\"expected_top\":\"command-doctor-helper\"` with `\"expected_top\":\"command-doctor-agents-md-check\"`. In the line with `\"id\":\"doctor-b-helper-handoff-02\"`, replace `\"expected_second\":\"command-doctor-helper\"` with `\"expected_second\":\"command-doctor-deep-loop\"`. In the line with `\"id\":\"doctor-b-helper-handoff-04\"`, replace `\"expected_top\":\"command-doctor-helper\"` with `\"expected_top\":\"command-doctor-setup\"`. Verify: `VDS` reports 0 failed, `rg -c '\"expected_top\":\"command-doctor-helper\"' $DP` prints 3, `rg -c '\"expected_second\":\"command-doctor-helper\"' $DP` prints 1 and `wc -l < $DP` prints 78.\n113: - [x] T007 [P] In `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md`, in the paragraph that starts `A doctor bridge passes on its own wording`, replace the text `` and if it does the `/doctor:helper` bridge passes so the operator is offered the command that names the right one. `` with the text `` and if it does the command the ranker puts first passes by name when its policy is `run`, and `/doctor:helper` passes instead when that command asks first or has no bridge. A prompt that asks for a `repair path` or says `I have a problem`, with no ranked command and no passing skill, gets `/doctor:helper`. `stopped converging` counts as a wrong state beside a passing skill. `` (both without the outer spaces). Verify: `rg -c \"repair path\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md` prints 1 and `rg -c \"is offered the command that names the right one\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md` prints nothing or 0.\n114: \n115: ### Wave A4\n116: - [x] T008 Rebuild and recapture after wave A (`BASE`). Run `BLD`, then `node $CAP --write`. Verify: `jq -c '.attachedMetrics.plain.tune' $BASE` prints `{\"own\":7,\"attached\":7,\"combined\":14,\"total\":45}` (expectation), `jq -r '.rows[\"cmd-doctor-agents-md-plain-tune-01\"].top, .rows[\"cmd-doctor-ci-plain-tune-01\"].top, .rows[\"cmd-doctor-helper-plain-tune-01\"].top, .rows[\"cmd-doctor-deep-loop-plain-tune-01\"].top3' $BASE` prints `command-doctor-agents-md-check`, `command-doctor-ci-report`, `command-doctor-helper` and `true`, `jq -c '.metrics.false_offer, .attachedMetrics.false_offer_attached' $BASE` prints `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}` twice and `RS` reports 0 failed. When the tune line differs from the expectation but the floors hold, write the actual line into `$SP/after-A.txt` in T009 and continue.\n117: \n118: ### Wave A5\n119: - [x] T009 Floor check after wave A (`$SP/after-A.txt`). Run `FLOORCHECK A`. Verify: every gate in `FLOORCHECK` prints what it must, and `diff <(rg '^(TYPED|EVAL): ' $SP/before.txt) <(rg '^(TYPED|EVAL): ' $SP/after-A.txt)` prints nothing, because the simulation moved no typed or scorer eval row. When a gate fails or that diff prints a line, mark T010 `[B]` with that line and stop.\n120: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 121]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/012-plain-offer-reach/tasks.md, lines 1-120\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Tasks: Phase 12: plain-offer-reach\"\n3: description: \"Ordered worker-sized tasks in five waves: name the matched doctor command in the hand-off, add sk-doc paraphrase aliases, label a hub that needs a mode, pair each deep mode with a scorer anchor and a hub alias and, only when the floors stay put, anchor three create rows. Each wave ends with a recapture and a floor check.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"plain offer reach tasks\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Tasks: Phase 12: plain-offer-reach\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n17: ## Task Notation\n18: \n19: | Prefix | Meaning |\n20: |--------|---------|\n21: | `[ ]` | Pending |\n22: | `[x]` | Completed |\n23: | `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n24: | `[B]` | Blocked |\n25: | `[C]` | Coordinator task: a decision, a revert, a live hook run or an operator step. No worker runs it |\n26: \n27: **Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n28: \n29: Every command runs from the repository root unless a task says otherwise.\n30: - `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. `TC` is `npm run typecheck` in `ADV`, which must exit 0. `BLD` is `npm run build` in `ADV`, which must exit 0. `SP` is this phase's `scratch/` folder.\n31: - `DH` is `$ADV/lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.ts` and `DHT` its test `$ADV/tests/doctor-helper-handoff.vitest.ts`. `VDHT` is `npx vitest run tests/doctor-helper-handoff.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n32: - `FU` is `$ADV/lib/scorer/fusion.ts`. `FHT` is `$ADV/tests/scorer/doctor-handoff-command.vitest.ts` (new) and `VFHT` is `npx vitest run tests/scorer/doctor-handoff-command.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n33: - `DP` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/doctor-prompts.jsonl`. `VDS` is `npx vitest run tests/doctor-routing-slice.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n34: - `CA` is `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` and `CAT` its test `$ADV/tests/command-attach.vitest.ts`. `VCA` is `npx vitest run tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` in `ADV`. `DBC` is `node $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs --check | jq -r .status`, which must print `fresh`.\n35: - `SCH` is `$ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` and `VSCH` is `npx vitest run tests/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.vitest.ts` in `ADV`. `SUB` is `$ADV/lib/subprocess.ts`.\n36: - `AR` is `$ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` and `ARC` its test `$ADV/tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts`. `VARC` is `npx vitest run tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n37: - `HFB` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts` and `HFT` its test `$ADV/tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts`. `VHFT` is `npx vitest run tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n38: - `RD` is `$ADV/lib/render.ts` and `GT` is `$ADV/tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts`. `VGT` is `npx vitest run tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts tests/command-head-length.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n39: - `EX` is `$ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/explicit.ts`. `VEX` is `npx vitest run tests/command-bridge-resolution-guard.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n40: - `HRD` is `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/hub-router.json` and `HRL` is `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/hub-router.json`. `CF_DOC` is `.skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/007-sk-doc/fixtures/canary-cases.v1.json` and `CF_LOOP` is `.skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/002-system-deep-loop/fixtures/canary-cases.v1.json`.\n41: - `MS` is `.skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/013-live-activation/activation` (the served manifests) and `MA` is `specs/sk-doc/z_archive/019-skill-routing-refactor/015-router-unification-program/013-live-activation/activation` (their authored twins).\n42: - `REFRESH <hub>` is three commands in order: `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route-manifest.cjs refresh --hub <hub> --skill-root .skilled/skills/<hub>`, then `cp $MS/<hub>/manifest.json $MA/<hub>/manifest.json`, then `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route-guard.cjs --json | jq .failures`, which must print `0`.\n43: - `HUBOK <hub>` is four checks: `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route-manifest.cjs freshness --hub <hub> --skill-root .skilled/skills/<hub> | jq -r .causeCode` prints `fresh`, `cmp $MS/<hub>/manifest.json $MA/<hub>/manifest.json` prints nothing, `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route-sync.cjs --check | tail -1` prints `all 55 served copies match their authored files` and `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/<hub> | tail -1` prints a line that starts with `OK: parent-skill-check`.\n44: - `BINT` is `node --test .skilled/bin/tests/compiled-route-*.test.cjs`, which must print `ℹ fail 0`.\n45: - `CAP` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`. `BASE` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json`. `CORPUS` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl`. `RS` is `npx vitest run tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n46: - `RT` is a shell function that prints the compiled route of every non-holdout corpus row and every canary prompt on one hub, as `<id><TAB>{\"action\":...,\"t\":[...]}`, and never prints a prompt. Define it in the shell first: `RT() { { jq -r 'select(.split!=\"holdout\") | [.id, .prompt] | @tsv' \"$CORPUS\"; jq -r '.cases[] | select(.prompt) | [\"canary:\" + .id, .prompt] | @tsv' \"$2\"; } | while IFS=$'\\t' read -r id p; do printf '%s\\t%s\\n' \"$id\" \"$(printf '%s' \"$p\" | node .skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub \"$1\" --prompt-stdin | jq -c '{action, t: [.targets[]? | .workflowMode]}')\"; done; }`. Call it as `RT sk-doc $CF_DOC` (154 lines) or `RT system-deep-loop $CF_LOOP` (139 lines).\n47: - `FLOOR` is `node $CAP | jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer'`, which must print at least `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` and exactly `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`.\n48: - `TYPED` is `node $CAP | jq -c '.attachedMetrics.false_offer_attached, .attachedMetrics.typed'`, which must print exactly `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}` and the typed line in `$SP/before.txt` (`{\"own\":24,\"attached\":20,\"combined\":44,\"total\":44}` once phase 011 is committed).\n49: - `PLAIN` is `node $CAP | jq -c '.attachedMetrics.plain.tune, .attachedMetrics.plain.holdout'`. It is a measurement, not a gate. The holdout line is a count and never a prompt.\n50: - `EVAL` is `node $ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs | jq -c '[.metrics.full_corpus_top1.correct,.metrics.holdout_top1.correct,.metrics.ambiguity_top1.correct,.metrics.gold_none_false_fire.value]'`, which must print numbers no lower than `[159,50,20]` and no lower than its line in `$SP/before.txt`, with the fourth no higher than 5.\n51: - `PY` is `python3 $ADV/tests/python/test_skill_advisor.py`, which must exit 0. `PAR` is `npx vitest run tests/parity/python-ts-parity.vitest.ts` in `ADV`, which must report 0 failed. `SUITE` is `npx vitest run` in `ADV`, whose `Test Files` and `Tests` summary lines must name no `failed` count.\n52: - `FLOORCHECK <X>` is: run `BLD`, then `FLOOR`, `TYPED`, `PLAIN`, `EVAL`, `TC`, `PY`, `PAR`, `RS`, `VDS`, `BINT`, `GUARD` (`node .skilled/bin/compiled-route-guard.cjs --json | jq .failures`) and `SUITE`, and write into `$SP/after-<X>.txt` one line per output line, each prefixed with the shorthand name and a colon, such as `FLOOR: {\"count\":0,\"total\":35}` or `TC: exit 0`. For the test runners write the summary line. It passes when every gate above prints what it must. `$SP/before.txt` uses the same format.\n53: \n54: Rules for every task:\n55: - Each task is one change to the files it names. A task that names a module and its test adds the behaviour and the cases that pin it.\n56: - No task reads or prints holdout prompt text. A script filters on `split` before it uses a prompt and prints row ids only. Tune and none rows may be read.\n57: - No code comment may name a spec path, a phase number, a task id, an ADR or a REQ id. State the durable reason instead. T032 checks it.\n58: - No task writes to the home folder, installs anything, adds a dependency, edits `AGENTS.md`, edits a file under `.skilled/commands/create/`, edits a `ROUTER.md` or edits a canary fixture.\n59: - A task that edits a hub `hub-router.json` ends with `REFRESH <hub>` and `HUBOK <hub>` in the same task.\n60: - The brief head keeps the phase 005 form. The `(needs a mode)` label is the one addition, and `GT` is re-pinned in the same task as the renderer.\n61: - A `.md` edit routes through `sk-doc` and a code edit through `sk-code` before the first write. Every task re-reads its anchor text first, because phase 011 edited the same files.\n62: \n63: Worker waves. Tasks in one wave touch different files and can run in parallel. Each task owns the files in parentheses. A wave starts only after the previous wave's last task printed its expected output.\n64: - Wave 0: T001 (`$SP/before.txt`), T002 (`$SP/routes-*-before.tsv`), T003 (`$SP/plain-before.json`). Read-only for the repository.\n65: - Gate: no task from wave A1 on starts before the coordinator confirms that phase 011 is committed, because it edits `CA`, `FU`, `AR`, `SCH`, `CAP` and `BASE`.\n66: - Wave A1: T004 (`DH`, `DHT`).\n67: - Wave A2: T005 (`FU`, `FHT`).\n68: - Wave A3: T006 (`DP`), T007 (the doctor feature catalog page).\n69: - Wave A4: T008 (`BASE`). Wave A5: T009 (`$SP/after-A.txt`).\n70: - Wave B1: T010 (`HRD`, both `sk-doc` manifests). Wave B2: T011 (`BASE`). Wave B3: T012 (`$SP/after-B.txt`).\n71: - Wave C1: T013 (`CA`, `CAT`), T014 (`SCH`), T015 (`SUB`).\n72: - Wave C2: T016 (`AR`, `ARC`), T017 (`RD`, `GT`).\n73: - Wave C3: T018 (`HFB`, `HFT`), T019 (the hook guide). Wave C4: T020 (`$SP/after-C.txt`).\n74: - Wave D1: T021 (`EX`), T022 (`HRL`, both deep-loop manifests). Wave D2: T023 (`BASE`). Wave D3: T024 (`$SP/after-D.txt`). Wave D4: T025 [C].\n75: - Wave E1: T026 (`EX`). Wave E2: T027 (`BASE`). Wave E3: T028 (`$SP/after-E.txt`). Wave E4: T029 [C].\n76: - Verification, one at a time: T030, T031, T032, T033 [C], T034.\n77: \n78: Expected plain tune line (`.attachedMetrics.plain.tune`) per wave. Only the floors are a hard gate:\n79: \n80: | After | own | attached | combined |\n81: |-------|-----|----------|----------|\n82: | Wave 0 | 2 | 7 | 9 |\n83: | A | 7 | 7 | 14 |\n84: | B | 7 | 10 | 17 |\n85: | C | 7 | 10 | 17 |\n86: | D | 7 | 13 | 20 |\n87: | E | 8 | 15 | 23 |\n88: <!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n89: \n90: ---\n91: \n92: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n93: ## Phase 1: Setup\n94: \n95: - [x] T001 Record the before numbers (`$SP/before.txt`). Run `BLD` only if `node $CAP` refuses a stale build, then run `FLOOR`, `TYPED`, `PLAIN`, `EVAL`, `TC`, `PY`, `PAR`, `RS`, `VDS`, `VCA`, `VGT`, `VDHT`, `VARC`, `VHFT`, `VSCH`, `VEX`, `DBC`, `BINT`, `SUITE`, `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route-guard.cjs --json | jq .failures`, `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route-sync.cjs --check | tail -1` and `HUBOK sk-doc` and `HUBOK system-deep-loop`, and write them into `before.txt` in the `FLOORCHECK` line format. Verify: `FLOOR` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `TYPED` prints `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}` and a typed line, `PLAIN` prints `{\"own\":2,\"attached\":7,\"combined\":9,\"total\":45}` first, `EVAL` prints numbers no lower than `[159,50,20]` with a fourth no higher than 5, `TC` and `PY` exit 0, the guard prints `0` and `wc -l < $SP/before.txt` prints at least 25. When a gate is red here, stop and mark the phase `[B]` with that line, because a red before number cannot be held. When `SUITE` names failed files, list them in `before.txt`, and from then on the `SUITE` gate is \"no failed file outside that list\".\n96: - [x] T002 Record every compiled route before any hub edit (`$SP/routes-sk-doc-before.tsv`, `$SP/routes-deep-loop-before.tsv`). Define `RT` and run `RT sk-doc $CF_DOC > $SP/routes-sk-doc-before.tsv` and `RT system-deep-loop $CF_LOOP > $SP/routes-deep-loop-before.tsv`. Verify: `wc -l < $SP/routes-sk-doc-before.tsv` prints 154, `wc -l < $SP/routes-deep-loop-before.tsv` prints 139, `rg -c 'holdout' $SP/routes-*-before.tsv` prints nothing or 0 for both and `rg -n '^nm-system-deep-loop-01' $SP/routes-deep-loop-before.tsv` prints `nm-system-deep-loop-01\t{\"action\":\"route\",\"t\":[\"research\"]}`.\n97: - [x] T003 Record each plain tune row's state (`$SP/plain-before.json`): run `node $CAP | jq '.attachedMetrics.attachedRows as $a | [.rows | to_entries[] | select(.key | test(\"plain-tune\")) | {id: .key, expected: .value.expected_command, top: .value.top, top1: .value.top1, top3: .value.top3, attached: ($a[.key] // null)}]' > $SP/plain-before.json`. Verify: `jq 'length' $SP/plain-before.json` prints 45, `jq '[.[] | select(.top1)] | length' $SP/plain-before.json` prints 2 and `jq -r '.[] | select(.id==\"cmd-doctor-ci-plain-tune-01\") | .top' $SP/plain-before.json` prints `command-doctor-helper`.\n98: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n99: \n100: ---\n101: \n102: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n103: ## Phase 2: Implementation\n104: \n105: ### Wave A1: the doctor hand-off module\n106: - [x] T004 Return the ranked runnable, add the gerund cue and add a repair request cue (`DH`, `DHT`). In `DH`: (1) in `interface HelperCandidate` add `readonly runnable?: string;` after `readonly command: string;`. (2) In `interface DoctorProblemMatch` add `readonly runnable: string;` after `readonly command: string;`, with the doc comment `` /** The command with its subcommand, such as `/doctor:agents-md check`. */ ``. (3) In `matchDoctorProblem`, change the returned object to `{ command: first.command, runnable: typeof first.runnable === 'string' && first.runnable !== '' ? first.runnable : first.command, score: first.score }`. (4) In `STRONG_PROBLEM_CUE`, add the line `  '\\\\bstopped converg\\\\w*\\\\b',` right after the line that starts `  '\\\\bnever (?:converg`. (5) After the `WEAK_PROBLEM_CUE` declaration add `const GENERIC_REPAIR_CUE = /\\b(?:repair path|i have a problem)\\b/i;` with the comment: a request for a repair route that names no problem the ranker knows still belongs to /doctor:helper, which lists the routes and their reasons, and the two phrases are exact so ordinary work requests never carry them. (6) After `doctorProblemCue` add `export function genericRepairCue(prompt: string): boolean { return GENERIC_REPAIR_CUE.test(prompt); }` with the doc comment `/** True when the prompt asks for a repair route without naming the problem. */`. (7) In the module header, replace `and if it does the advisor offers` and the line after it, `/doctor:helper, which then names the command.`, with `and if it does the advisor offers the command the ranker named, or` and `/doctor:helper when that command asks before it runs.`. In `DHT` add cases: `doctorProblemCue('my research loop stopped converging and I cannot see why')` is `'strong'`, `matchDoctorProblem('confirm the AGENTS.md sections in this repo have not drifted', WORKSPACE)?.runnable` is `'/doctor:agents-md check'`, `matchDoctorProblem('show me every GitHub Actions workflow and whether each is enabled', WORKSPACE)?.runn... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n107: \n108: ### Wave A2: the hand-off inserts the named command\n109: - [x] T005 Insert the ranked `run` command instead of the helper (`FU`, `FHT`). In `FU`: (1) add `COMMAND_ROWS` to the import from `'../command-attach.js'` and `genericRepairCue` to the import from `'./doctor-helper-handoff.js'`. (2) Right above the comment block that precedes `export function applyDoctorHelperHandoff(`, add `export function runnableDoctorBridgeId(runnable: string, projection: AdvisorProjection): string | undefined` with this body: for each `[id, row]` of `Object.entries(COMMAND_ROWS)`, skip it unless `id.startsWith(DOCTOR_BRIDGE_PREFIX)`, `row.command === runnable` and `row.policy === 'run'`, and return `id` when `projection.skills.some((skill) => skill.id === id)`. After the loop return `undefined`. Its comment says the ranker names a runnable such as `/doctor:agents-md check`, and this returns that bridge when it runs without asking and the projection holds it. (3) Replace the four comment lines above `applyDoctorHelperHandoff` with: `// A doctor problem described in other words than a bridge's own phrases reaches`, `// no doctor bridge. When none passes and none was typed, /doctor:helper's ranker`, `// decides whether the prompt is a doctor problem. If it is, the command it ranks`, `// first passes when that command runs without asking, and the helper passes`, `// otherwise. A plain request for a repair route with no ranked command and no`, `// passing skill also gets the helper.`. (4) In the function, replace `if (!match) return [...ranked];` with `if (!match && (skillPasses || !genericRepairCue(context.prompt))) return [...ranked];`, and prefix the next condition with `match && ` so it reads `if (match && cue === null && match.score < DOCTOR_HELPER_UNCUED_MIN_SCORE) return [...ranked];`. (5) Before `const existing =` add `const handoffId = (match ? runnableDoctorBridgeId(match.runnable, context.projection) : undefined) ?? DOCTOR_HELPER_BRIDGE_ID;` and `const handoffSkill = context.projection.skills.find((skill) => skill.id === handoffId) ?? he... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n110: \n111: ### Wave A3\n112: - [x] T006 [P] Relabel the three hand-off rows that now get a named command (`DP`). Change exactly three lines and nothing else. In the line with `\"id\":\"doctor-b-helper-handoff-01\"`, replace `\"expected_top\":\"command-doctor-helper\"` with `\"expected_top\":\"command-doctor-agents-md-check\"`. In the line with `\"id\":\"doctor-b-helper-handoff-02\"`, replace `\"expected_second\":\"command-doctor-helper\"` with `\"expected_second\":\"command-doctor-deep-loop\"`. In the line with `\"id\":\"doctor-b-helper-handoff-04\"`, replace `\"expected_top\":\"command-doctor-helper\"` with `\"expected_top\":\"command-doctor-setup\"`. Verify: `VDS` reports 0 failed, `rg -c '\"expected_top\":\"command-doctor-helper\"' $DP` prints 3, `rg -c '\"expected_second\":\"command-doctor-helper\"' $DP` prints 1 and `wc -l < $DP` prints 78.\n113: - [x] T007 [P] In `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md`, in the paragraph that starts `A doctor bridge passes on its own wording`, replace the text `` and if it does the `/doctor:helper` bridge passes so the operator is offered the command that names the right one. `` with the text `` and if it does the command the ranker puts first passes by name when its policy is `run`, and `/doctor:helper` passes instead when that command asks first or has no bridge. A prompt that asks for a `repair path` or says `I have a problem`, with no ranked command and no passing skill, gets `/doctor:helper`. `stopped converging` counts as a wrong state beside a passing skill. `` (both without the outer spaces). Verify: `rg -c \"repair path\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md` prints 1 and `rg -c \"is offered the command that names the right one\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md` prints nothing or 0.\n114: \n115: ### Wave A4\n116: - [x] T008 Rebuild and recapture after wave A (`BASE`). Run `BLD`, then `node $CAP --write`. Verify: `jq -c '.attachedMetrics.plain.tune' $BASE` prints `{\"own\":7,\"attached\":7,\"combined\":14,\"total\":45}` (expectation), `jq -r '.rows[\"cmd-doctor-agents-md-plain-tune-01\"].top, .rows[\"cmd-doctor-ci-plain-tune-01\"].top, .rows[\"cmd-doctor-helper-plain-tune-01\"].top, .rows[\"cmd-doctor-deep-loop-plain-tune-01\"].top3' $BASE` prints `command-doctor-agents-md-check`, `command-doctor-ci-report`, `command-doctor-helper` and `true`, `jq -c '.metrics.false_offer, .attachedMetrics.false_offer_attached' $BASE` prints `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}` twice and `RS` reports 0 failed. When the tune line differs from the expectation but the floors hold, write the actual line into `$SP/after-A.txt` in T009 and continue.\n117: \n118: ### Wave A5\n119: - [x] T009 Floor check after wave A (`$SP/after-A.txt`). Run `FLOORCHECK A`. Verify: every gate in `FLOORCHECK` prints what it must, and `diff <(rg '^(TYPED|EVAL): ' $SP/before.txt) <(rg '^(TYPED|EVAL): ' $SP/after-A.txt)` prints nothing, because the simulation moved no typed or scorer eval row. When a gate fails or that diff prints a line, mark T010 `[B]` with that line and stop.\n120: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 121]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/012-plain-offer-reach/tasks.md\",\"limit\":120}"},"time":{"start":1794544201777,"end":1794544202277}}}}
